--- make
description: A .env file of NAME=value secrets: .env, or .env.<env> for one environment; never served
category: Settings
usage: <base|environment> [--keys API_TOKEN,DATABASE_URL]
--keys: The variable names to add, comma separated (default API_TOKEN)
example: kscript make env base --keys API_TOKEN,DATABASE_URL
example: kscript make env staging
to: .env{{#unless name in base, default, env}}.{{ kebab }}{{/unless}}
hint: Keep it out of git (add .env* to .gitignore). Read a value with @env('NAME') or $config; the auth middleware reads API_TOKEN
---
# {{#if name in base, default, env}}Secrets for every environment{{else}}Secrets for {{ kebab }} (kscript --env {{ kebab }}), laid over .env{{/if}}.
# NAME=value lines; they become environment variables unless one is already set. Don't commit this file.
{{#each keys}}
{{ item | upper }}=
{{else}}
API_TOKEN=
{{/each}}
